## 3. Accessibility, Contrast & Readability Fixes

We have resolved all WCAG 2.1 AA compliance, colorblindness (CVD), and projector/beamer readability issues across the presentation dashboard:

1. **Heading Readability:** Replaced the CSS text-gradient clip effect (`-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent`) with a solid high-contrast celestial Sky Blue (`#0ea5e9`) for all `h1` through `h6` tags. This prevents browser rendering bugs and text washing out on projectors, making the titles vibrant and easy to read.
2. **Table Readability & Background Isolation:** Wrapped custom HTML tables (the Hypothesis table in [tab_0.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_0.py) and the Reviewer scorecard in [tab_3.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_3.py)) inside `glass-card` containers to guarantee a dark slate background, and explicitly styled rows and cells with `color: COLOR_PALETTE['text']` (`#f1f5f9`).
3. **HTML Indentation Fix:** Left-aligned all HTML strings inside Python `f"""` blocks. Indenting them previously caused Streamlit's Markdown parser to treat them as preformatted code blocks (`<pre><code>`), exposing raw tags (like `</tbody>` and `</table>`) on the user interface.
4. **Card Text Legibility:** Configured a CSS rule forcing paragraph (`p`) and list (`li`, `ul`, `ol`) text inside `.glass-card` elements to use a light slate color (`#e2e8f0`) globally in `styles.css`. This prevents elements (like the Toulmin framework card content and the Passive Copier stats) from inheriting dark default text colors from Light Mode environments.
5. **Contrast Compliance & Colorblindness Safety:**
   - Lightened `text_muted` to `#b0bec5` inside the card elements (raising contrast above the 4.5:1 ratio).
   - Increased active tab selection background opacity from `0.15` to `0.30` in [styles.css](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/styles.css) for better text contrast.
   - Increased `.glass-card` background opacity to `0.88` to ensure it is visible and crisp on projectors.
   - Changed Plotly Treatment color (`ai`) to `#38bdf8` (passing contrast AA).
   - Changed Plotly `success` to `#f59e0b` (Amber) and `warning` to `#fb923c` (Orange) in [config.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/config.py) to eliminate red-green (deuteranopia) conflicts against the control rose color (`no_ai`, `#f43f5e`).
   - Changed `.badge-sig` style from green to blue (`#60a5fa` text on `rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.15)` bg) and lightened `.badge-non-sig` text color to `#f87171` to ensure they are distinct for colorblind users and highly visible on beamers.
6. **Academic Paper Metadata Integration:** Integrated the official paper details into the header in [app.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/app.py) and the title card in [tab_0.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_0.py), showing Paper ID `854 / PAR-T9.3-2: 2`, Track `9.3: "AI in the Lab..."`, Title `"The Efficiency Illusion..."`, Author `"Bonazzi, Riccardo"`, and the list of keywords.


